<Base title="Privacy & Terms | Quilt Cut Planner" description="Read Quilt Cut Planner privacy practices, browser-local project data handling and plain-language terms for using the free cutting calculators.">
<div class="page-shell"><div class="page-heading"><span class="eyebrow-with-line">— PRIVACY AT THE CUTTING TABLE</span><h1>Privacy and terms for using Quilt Cut Planner.</h1><p>Here is how the browser handles your project measurements and the practical terms that apply when using these free cutting estimates.</p></div>
<section class="content-block"><div class="story-grid">
<article class="story-panel"><h2>Where are project measurements stored?</h2><p>When you change project inputs, the tool may store a versioned JSON project in your browser's localStorage, so dimensions can carry between calculators. You can reset the sample, clear your browser data or save a JSON file yourself.</p></article>
<article class="story-panel"><h2>How do import and export files work?</h2><p>The file import control reads your selected JSON file inside your browser. The save and cut-plan buttons create files on your device; no project file is sent to a Quilt Cut Planner account or server.</p></article>
<article class="story-panel"><h2>What hosting and future services are involved?</h2><p>Normal requests to load website pages and images may be recorded by the hosting provider. The initial code has no advertising or analytics integrations. If either is enabled later, this statement and applicable consent controls must be reviewed first.</p></article>
</div></section>
<section class="content-block" id="usage-terms" aria-label="Use and responsibility">
 <h2>What are the terms for using these calculators?</h2>
 <p>By using these tools, you agree to treat results as planning estimates rather than guaranteed cutting instructions, professional sewing advice or an independent certification. Check every dimension, usable fabric width, grain direction, seam allowance, print scale and material label before buying or cutting. You are responsible for confirming that the plan matches your pattern, machine, fabric and construction method.</p>
 <p>We aim to correct documented calculation defects. For a reproducible issue, see the <a href="/about/#editorial">project attribution and corrections policy</a> and the linked source repository. Nothing on this site represents a professional warranty of fit, sewing performance or retailer pricing.</p>
</section>
<p class="footer-note">Current code policy last reviewed November 2026. This statement describes our current browser-only production tools. We will review it before introducing advertising, analytics or additional data processing. See the <a href="https://github.com/garrison2025/Quilt_Calculator">source repository</a> for implementation details.</p></div>
</Base>
